  "description": "Below is a concise reference for two basic Arabic letters:\n\n- The first entry concerns **Arabic Letter Alef** (U+0627). Its printed form is \u201c\u0627\u201d, and it is transliterated as **a**. This character belongs to the tags *Arabic* and *Letter*. In isolated and initial positions it appears as \u201c\u0627\u201d, while in the final position it takes the shape \u201c\ufe8e\u201d and in medial position it is rendered as \u201c\u0640\u0627\u201d.\n\n- The second entry describes **Arabic Letter Beh** (U+0628). Its glyph is \u201c\u0628\u201d, with the transliteration **b**, and it shares the same tags, *Arabic* and *Letter*. It also uses \u201c\u0628\u201d for both isolated and initial forms; its final form is displayed as \u201c\ufe92\u201d, and the medial form connects as \u201c\u0640\u0628\u201d.",
